@startuml
title UML sequence - Internal payment, action approval and acknowledgement recovery
actor Payer
actor Recipient
participant "Customer web / BFF" as API
participant "Payments" as Payments
participant "Identity / issuer" as IAM
participant "Controls" as Controls
participant "Platform workflow" as Jobs
participant "Worker" as Worker
participant "Core" as Core
Recipient -> Core : Issue shareable receiving reference as current owner
Recipient --> Payer : Share opaque reference
Payer -> API : Register recipient / request exact quote
API -> Payments : Current owned source + receiving reference + amount
Payments -> Core : Resolve active receiver and source product policy
Core --> Payments : Exact versioned price / limits / destination
Payments -> Payments : Immutable quote and one payment identity
Payer -> API : Review / create intent using stable request key
API -> Payments : Bind one immutable quote to one intent
Payments -> Controls : Action challenge binds exact PaymentDetails
Payer -> IAM : Fresh OIDC authorization code / PKCE / nonce
IAM -> IAM : Expected actor + auth_time + details-bound proof
Payer -> API : Confirm original intent and quote
API -> Payments : Current source / recipient / quote guards
Payments -> Controls : Consume original action-bound proof
Payments -> Payments : Commit ACCEPTED intent and audit/outbox intent
Payments -> Jobs : Accept stable workflow / original payment ID
Jobs --> API : Saved operation identity
Worker -> Jobs : Claim lease / fence
Worker -> Payments : Process original payment
Payments -> Payments : Serialize intent and recipient revocation
Payments -> Controls : Current permission, action proof and signed checks
alt Current denial / expiry / blocked instruction
 Payments -> Payments : Record nonexecution outcome; no journal effect
else Current pending / review
 Payments -> Jobs : Retry or owned review; preserve original identity
else Current gates allow execution
 Payments -> Core : Bound InternalInstruction + trusted expiring permit
 Core -> Core : Lock accounts in UUID order
 Core -> Core : Recheck expiry, restrictions, exact fee, funds and daily principal limit
 group One Core transaction
  Core -> Core : Debit total / credit recipient / credit fee account
  Core -> Core : Balanced journal + immutable execution receipt + outbox
 end
 alt Lost acknowledgement
  Core --x Payments : Response unavailable after commit
  Worker -> Payments : Retry original payment
  Payments -> Core : Retrieve receipt by original identity + full request digest
  Core --> Payments : Original journal batch
 else Acknowledgement received
  Core --> Payments : Journal batch evidence
 end
 Payments -> Payments : Commit SETTLED + event / audit intent
end
Payments -> Controls : Relay persisted audit record with stable ID
Payer -> API : Resume / refresh original payment
API -> Payments : Current authorized inquiry
Payments --> Payer : Actual status, fees, date and original booking reference
note over Payments,Core
Payment ID is the economic business identity.
Platform workflow ID is a distinct scheduling identity.
No external provider acknowledgement is used as internal settlement evidence.
end note
@enduml
